uts with a non-zero embedded LZMA initial byte.","evidence":["The new public constant and set_quirk! branch create a configuration action absent in S0.","The changed conditional `(c8 <> 0x00) and not this.allow_non_zero_initial_byte` creates input-dependent behavior requiring control of both the quirk state and initial byte.","The Lzip decoder newly calls set_quirk! with this quirk before transform_io?."]},"explicit_failure":false,"delta_attribution":"NEW","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"reason":"Within the stable scope of the newly added LZMA quirk and corresponding non-zero-initial-byte semantics, S0 had no such configurable behavior to expose, while S1 does. H0 remains JSON-only and cannot enable the configuration or construct inputs for the affected LZMA/Lzip entry points. This is a concrete new configuration and input-construction obligation, so the delta is NEW."}
